# macOS shadcn components

Controls should read as macOS, not generic Material/shadcn defaults.

## Do

- Height ~28px, radius ~6px, `os-chrome` / 13px SF-like type
- Fills: `var(--control-fill)` / hover `var(--control-fill-hover)` — classes `.macos-input`, `.macos-select`, `.macos-button`
- Focus ring: accent mix, e.g. `color-mix(in srgb, var(--macos-accent) 35%, transparent)`
- Primary actions / checked switch / selected radio / menu highlight: `var(--macos-accent)`
- Select trigger: double chevron (`ChevronsUpDown`), not a single chevron
- Switch: 38×21 pill, white thumb; Radio: filled accent circle with white center dot
- Popovers/menus: translucent `bg-popover` + backdrop blur; item focus `bg-[var(--macos-accent)] text-white`

## Don't

- Hardcode blue hex for selection/focus
- Use tall Material-style inputs (h-10+) for OS chrome
- Rely on opaque white-only surfaces that ignore Liquid Glass / dark mode
